# Per-file policy for sync-public.sh (private pi-setup -> public pi-setup-public).
#
# Format: <policy> <glob>
#   never        tracked here, must NEVER reach the public repo
#   keep-public  public's own version wins; private changes are ignored
#   public-only  exists only in public; never delete it
#
# Anything tracked and unmatched is synced private -> public.
#
# SAFETY LAYERS (all must hold, the script enforces each):
#   1. Source is `git ls-files` only. Gitignored paths - every work-IP skill,
#      every .env, the db-intelligence domain pack - are structurally
#      unreachable, not merely filtered.
#   2. `never` removes private-but-tracked files (memory, its sync plumbing).
#   3. A domain-identifier assertion runs over the final file set AND the
#      staged diff. Any hit aborts before anything is committed.
#   4. The script stages only. A human reviews `git diff --cached` and pushes.

# ---- never: private work knowledge and its plumbing ----
never  memory/**
never  sync-memory.sh
never  configs/com.cskwork.pi-memory-sync.plist
never  skills/db-intelligence/reference/domain/**

# ---- keep-public: deliberately sanitized, public version is authoritative ----
# .gitignore      - public says "PUBLIC replica"; private lists work-IP skills
# README*.md      - public quick start clones pi-setup-public; private clones pi-setup
# sync.sh         - public uses YOUR-COMPANY placeholders; private uses real
#                   employer/project keywords. Publishing private would leak
#                   the exact identifiers the tripwire exists to hide.
# pi-settings     - public documents the public repo; private documents memory
keep-public  .gitignore
keep-public  README.md
keep-public  README.ko.md
keep-public  sync.sh
keep-public  skills/pi-settings/SKILL.md
keep-public  .github/workflows/check-docs.yml

# ---- public-only: landing page and link check, private has no copy ----
public-only  docs/**
public-only  scripts/check-public-links.sh
